**Diagnosis:** `median` in `src.js` returned `sorted[Math.floor(len / 2)]` unconditionally. For even-length arrays that is the upper-middle element, so `median([1,2,3,4])` returned `3` instead of `2.5`.

**Fix (src.js only):**
```js
export function median(numbers) {
  const sorted = [...numbers].sort((a, b) => a - b)
  const mid = Math.floor(sorted.length / 2)
  if (sorted.length % 2 === 0) return (sorted[mid - 1] + sorted[mid]) / 2
  return sorted[mid]
}
```

