**Diagnosis:** `src.js` implemented `deepEqual` as `a === b`. Under `===`, `NaN === NaN` is `false`, so `deepEqual(NaN, NaN)` returned `false` and failed the `treats NaN as equal` assertion.

**Fix (only `src.js`):**
```js
export function deepEqual(a, b) {
  if (a === b) return true
  // NaN is the only value not equal to itself under ===
  return Number.isNaN(a) && Number.isNaN(b)
}
```

This keeps the original `===` behavior for all other values (including `0`/`-0` and distinct object references) and only adds the NaN self-equality special case. `test.js` was not modified.
